  "what": "problem PD-1@v1 drafted",
  "phase": "DISCOVER",
  "minute": 55.0,
  "event_seq": 103,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets at Lakeside Water Utility doubled from ~600/month to ~1,200-1,260/month between July and August-September 2026 (E-07) because manual meter-reading route completion fell to 88% against a 95% target over that window, covering 9,200 manual-read accounts (E-02); the resulting missed field reads trigger estimate substitution in the billing import step, and this substitution channel accounts for the 41% of disputed bills that were on ESTIMATED reads (E-04), producing inaccurate bills that drive a material share of the dispute surge. Response-handling speed is not the mechanism, since dispute response times remain within SLA throughout the surge (E-01)."
 },
